WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8959515Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8969569Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8970418Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8971074Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8971384Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8971618Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8972223Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8972538Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8973186Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8973551Z 
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8973706Z If you would like to
WebUI i18n health	Install Nix	2026-10-12T21:38:12.8974104Z see the output, try like this:
